\pard\plain \fi720\sl288\slmult1\ltrch\loch {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 It would take a deft hand to capture her smirk. Difficult, but doable. The rest of the room was full of subtleties which could not be captured in a painting. The cool, dark grays called for a shade of blue which he\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92d never been able to find. The blackwood floor creaked under his step, and that sound, the sensitivity of it\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 a slight toe-pressure and out came crreeeeeeak\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 that tactile age, the humidity, could only be suggested. And then the tall window set into the middle of the wall shot breakfast sunbeams all the way across the room, slanting up the opposite wall, and that golden light was alive with dust motes which swam up towards the ceiling, fleeing him. The ceiling itself sagged and cracked, as though the plastered clay were as old as she was.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 She sat in the darkest corner, aged hands folded in her lap. She was wrapped in a black shawl like a mourner. Her double-winged chair loomed over her, and the look she gave him, with her filmy eyes, if he were to paint it, he\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92d paint it saying, \u8220\'93I\u8217\'92m sorry you have to see me like this.\u8221\'94 And then that smirk said something like, \u8220\'93If you\u8217\'92d known me when I was younger, when I was prettier and vibrant, then we would might have been friends, maybe more, but I understand that you want nothing to do with me, and honestly, I don\u8217\'92t want anything to do with you because life hasn\u8217\'92t stabbed you in the gut and so you don\u8217\'92t really know who you are yet.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 She might not have been thinking that. She probably wasn\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t. An old woman had told him that once, and so he assumed that every old woman with a natural lightness was thinking that. But then her mood shifted, and her smirk alighted, a sudden smile, as though suddenly remembering her manners.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93You must be the painter,\u8221\'94 she said, voice clearer than expected. \u8220\'93Your name?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Mandri,\u8221\'94 he replied.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Mandriiii,\u8221\'94 she said with a grandmothering lilt. \u8220\'93Yes. Come in, come in, come in. The young Vigram craves your indulgence in the dining room.\u8221\'94  She pushed herself up and out of her chair, straining with the effort, making him feel awkward for not offering to help. Once standing, she was firm on her feet.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I am Pel,\u8221\'94 she said.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Are you Vigram\u8217\'92s mother?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 She shook her head. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I am not certain of our relation.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 Which was much the same as the living room, an ambient light strewing throughonly longer, with a long, blackwood table dominating the . The light came courtesy of the }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 She held out her crinkly hand and \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93The dining room.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1}